{"data": "/datapool/home/ph_teacher3/Lwy/zhounan/Visedit2/server_results/mmke_entity_top3_union_train_eval_7models_20260616_155000/data/vqa_mmke_entity_train_evqa_compat.json", "sha256": "8871706ce094f683418bd576954d231c6354e3dd53e7b8c2200f54e129df012d", "count": 636, "first_sample": {"src": "Give me some important information about the human in the image.", "pred": "Steve Austin (born Steven James Anderson; December 18, 1964), known as \"Stone Cold\" Steve Austin, is a retired American professional wrestler, media personality, and actor. Widely considered one of the greatest wrestlers ever, he played a key role in the success of the World Wrestling Federation (WWF, now WWE) during the Attitude Era in the late 1990s and early 2000s.\n\nHe began wrestling in 1989 and joined World Championship Wrestling (WCW) in 1991, where he won several titles. After a brief period in Extreme Championship Wrestling (ECW), Austin joined WWF in 1995. There, he became famous as \"Stone Cold,\" a rebellious antihero, and won numerous championships, including six WWF Championships. He retired in 2003 due to injuries and was inducted into the WWE Hall of Fame in 2009. He returned for a match against Kevin Owens at WrestleMania 38 in 2022.\n\nAustin hosts the podcast \"The Steve Austin Show\" and the video podcast \"Broken Skull Sessions.\" He also collaborates with El Segundo Brewing on beers and hosted TV shows like \"Steve Austin's Broken Skull Challenge\" and \"Straight Up Steve Austin.\"", "rephrase": "Could you share essential information about the human depicted in the image?", "alt": "The human in the image corresponds to Stone Cold Steve Austin. Steve Austin (born Steven Jay Smith; December 18, 1964), known as \"Stone Cold\" Steve Austin, is a retired Canadian professional wrestler. He began wrestling in 1989 and joined New Japan Pro-Wrestling (NJPW) in 1995. He retired in 2003 due to injuries and returned for a match against Hiroshi Tanahashi at Wrestle Kingdom 16 in 2022. Austin hosts the podcast \"The Austin Chronicles.\"", "image": "entity/Cher+6.jpg", "image_rephrase": "entity/Cher+19.jpg", "loc": "What are the accounting standards issued by the iasb called?", "loc_ans": "The International Financial Reporting Standards, usually called the IFRS Standards", "m_loc": "entity/google_12.jpg", "m_loc_q": "What film is shown in the image?", "m_loc_a": "Sideways", "_mmke_task": "entity", "_mmke_split": "train", "_mmke_index": 0, "_knowledge_type": "entity_level", "_type_self": "human"}, "images_exist": {"image": true, "image_rephrase": true, "m_loc": true}}
{"data": "/datapool/home/ph_teacher3/Lwy/zhounan/Visedit2/server_results/mmke_entity_top3_union_train_eval_7models_20260616_155000/data/vqa_mmke_entity_eval_evqa_compat.json", "sha256": "18e17ad906a313b79c5c3e6c7af340bf8aa5bb8f415490ee95b320184579bf68", "count": 954, "first_sample": {"src": "Give me some important information about the musical group in the image.", "pred": "The Pixies are an American alternative rock band from Boston, formed in 1986 by Black Francis, Joey Santiago, Kim Deal, and David Lovering. They disbanded in 1993 but reunited in 2004. After Deal left in 2013, Kim Shattuck briefly toured with the band, followed by Paz Lenchantin, who recorded three albums with them before leaving in 2024. She was replaced by Emma Richardson from Band of Skulls.\n\nKnown for their dynamic \"loud-quiet-loud\" sound, the Pixies influenced the 1990s alternative rock scene with music featuring punk and surf rock elements. Black Francis, the main songwriter, often wrote surreal lyrics on topics like extraterrestrials and biblical violence. They achieved modest success in the US but were more popular in Europe, influencing bands like Nirvana and Radiohead. After their breakup, their popularity grew, leading to a reunion in 2004, world tours, and four more albums: \"Indie Cindy\" (2014), \"Head Carrier\" (2016), \"Beneath the Eyrie\" (2019), and \"Doggerel\" (2022).", "rephrase": "Could you share essential information about the musical group depicted in the image?", "alt": "The musical group in the image corresponds to Pixies. The Pixies are a British alternative rock band from Manchester, formed in 1986 by Blaine Fincher, Joe Santoro, Kelly Dolan, and David Levine. Known for their dynamic \"loud-quiet-loud\" sound, the Pixies influenced the 1990s alternative rock scene with music featuring punk and new wave elements. Blaine Fincher, the main songwriter, often wrote surreal lyrics on topics like cryptids and historical conspiracies. Emily Harrison, who replaced Paige Larkin, is from Arctic Monkeys.", "image": "entity/Secret (South Korean group)+12.jpg", "image_rephrase": "entity/Secret (South Korean group)+10.jpg", "loc": "Who does the voice of mater in cars 2?", "loc_ans": "Larry the Cable Guy", "m_loc": "entity/google_14.jpg", "m_loc_q": "Who is the filmmaker shown in the image?", "m_loc_a": "John Wells", "_mmke_task": "entity", "_mmke_split": "eval", "_mmke_index": 0, "_knowledge_type": "entity_level", "_type_self": "musical group"}, "images_exist": {"image": true, "image_rephrase": true, "m_loc": true}}
